I just assumed like, oh, these are videos he's done.

2515
01:55:32,960 --> 01:55:35,380
But it would be like, hey, Nick, okay.

2516
01:55:35,380 --> 01:55:38,079
Room three is the car.

2517
01:55:38,079 --> 01:55:39,340
And I would be like, oh my God,

2518
01:55:39,340 --> 01:55:42,859
he made all of the videos for me.

2519
01:55:42,859 --> 01:55:45,179
And then I got to the spreadsheets and the insurance,

2520
01:55:45,180 --> 01:55:51,360
all that. And a lot of that was like verifiably, like kind of wrong, but here he was doing it all.

2521
01:55:51,360 --> 01:55:56,840
Like it wasn't just like a business plan of like the thing he was great at. It included all of the

2522
01:55:56,840 --> 01:56:02,740
things to do a proof of concept that this would indeed be a great business. And I had put a limit,

2523
01:56:02,900 --> 01:56:08,079
a bottom line. I said, look, if you build something like that, it can't gross under 20 million.

2524
01:56:08,640 --> 01:56:11,960
Like it sounds like a big number, but like when you do the throughput and the math,

2525
01:56:11,960 --> 01:56:15,800
It's actually not that big of a number at $120 ticket price or something.

2526
01:56:16,399 --> 01:56:18,500
And that's what it is, you know?

2527
01:56:18,659 --> 01:56:21,539
And I started going through like whenever I go to like the sphere, I'm like,

2528
01:56:21,640 --> 01:56:23,000
what are the economics of the sphere?

2529
01:56:23,000 --> 01:56:23,199
Right?

2530
01:56:23,199 --> 01:56:24,300
You know, I can't help myself.

2531
01:56:24,300 --> 01:56:24,640
You're not watching the show.

2532
01:56:24,640 --> 01:56:25,539
I can't help myself.

2533
01:56:25,539 --> 01:56:26,039
Right.

2534
01:56:26,039 --> 01:56:28,300
So it was a great business plan.

2535
01:56:28,539 --> 01:56:32,020
And by the time he got out of the Canadian wild, I had read it like three times.

2536
01:56:32,520 --> 01:56:35,060
And my first thing I said to him, I was like, this is the last thing

2537
01:56:35,060 --> 01:56:39,279
I need in my life right now, but there's no way we can't do this.

2538
01:56:39,279 --> 01:56:39,579
Right.

2539
01:56:39,579 --> 01:56:41,319
And that was three years ago.

2540
01:56:41,319 --> 01:56:46,079
And in the past three years, we have scoured the world for real estate

2541
01:56:46,079 --> 01:56:48,000
because the real estate is the thing you get married to.

2542
01:56:48,079 --> 01:56:49,259
It's like the Ray Kroc story.

2543
01:56:49,259 --> 01:56:50,920
Like they're not in the business of selling hamburgers.

2544
01:56:51,219 --> 01:56:52,279
They're in the business of real estate.

2545
01:56:52,599 --> 01:56:56,319
I learned long ago that the deal that you make for a restaurant

2546
01:56:56,319 --> 01:56:59,359
or for a show or whatever, in this case,

2547
01:56:59,399 --> 01:57:01,259
