2548
01:57:01,519 --> 01:57:03,599
You are building a purpose-built theater.

2549
01:57:03,859 --> 01:57:05,199
That is a small high hoop.

2550
01:57:05,599 --> 01:57:07,380
There are very few people that are going to do that.

2551
01:57:07,679 --> 01:57:10,859
And I knew the guys for years who did Sleep No More.

2552
01:57:11,319 --> 01:57:17,859
And Sleep No More was a similar idea where traditionally the theater is you sit in a chair, it's happening on the stage.

2553
01:57:18,019 --> 01:57:20,699
You watch the thing, show's over.

2554
01:57:20,960 --> 01:57:27,059
Sleep No More was like you go to this hotel, motel, and the play is happening in and around you.

2555
01:57:27,099 --> 01:57:27,920
And it makes no sense.

2556
01:57:28,119 --> 01:57:28,819
It's not linear.

2557
01:57:29,119 --> 01:57:29,819
It's not like it can't.

2558
01:57:29,819 --> 01:57:31,659
Because you go to a different room, a different scene is going on.

2559
01:57:31,779 --> 01:57:32,420
I don't know what the hell's happening.

2560
01:57:32,679 --> 01:57:34,699
They're dancing, not talking, and it's Hamlet.

2561
01:57:35,099 --> 01:57:37,019
But the thing was like, it was sold out.

2562
01:57:37,079 --> 01:57:38,639
It made like hundreds of millions in revenue, right?

2563
01:57:38,679 --> 01:57:39,119
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

2564
01:57:39,119 --> 01:57:44,099
Yeah. And it also like the first time I did it, it was like nothing I'd ever seen. And while this

2565
01:57:44,099 --> 01:57:52,619
is different because it utilizes illusion to create that sense of childlike wonder and awe

2566
01:57:52,619 --> 01:57:56,380
that we were talking about earlier. Right. And that's what we were trying to do with Alenia.

2567
01:57:56,380 --> 01:57:57,019
That's the cheese.

2568
01:57:57,359 --> 01:57:57,899
That's the cheese.

2569
01:57:57,899 --> 01:57:59,479
That's the customer's cheese.

2570
01:58:00,019 --> 01:58:00,300
Yeah.

2571
01:58:00,500 --> 01:58:01,140
A moment of wonder.

2572
01:58:01,140 --> 01:58:09,039
And I would say that as much as I love AI and I live mostly here, I would like to connect my

2573
01:58:09,039 --> 01:58:13,500
body more to my mind. Like, you know, like, like I'm not as disciplined about exercise as I should

2574
01:58:13,500 --> 01:58:18,479
be and things like that. But theater, great theater, great music is about human connection

2575
01:58:18,479 --> 01:58:28,180
and utilizing illusion now in an immersive thing that you cannot get any other way feels like it's

2576
01:58:28,180 --> 01:58:31,979
going to be more important two years from now than it is less important two years from now.

2577
01:58:31,979 --> 01:58:37,680
Yeah. Because more and more and more things are going to go the AI route. They're going to go in

2578
01:58:37,680 --> 01:58:41,159
the non-person, you know, they don't need to be person to person anymore.

2579
01:58:41,400 --> 01:58:42,659
Agents are going to be doing things.

2580
01:58:42,720 --> 01:58:43,640
I love all that.

2581
01:58:43,680 --> 01:58:45,060
I am all in on all of it.

2582
01:58:45,579 --> 01:58:48,440
I still believe that sitting down to a table is important.

2583
01:58:48,480 --> 01:58:51,420
I still believe that growing the wine in 10 years is important.

2584
01:58:51,900 --> 01:58:57,000
And I want to create human connection among complete strangers because you

2585
01:58:57,000 --> 01:58:58,720
don't meet, people don't meet each other anymore.

2586
01:58:58,820 --> 01:59:04,360
And all the discourse is that's an other, that person's an other.

2587
01:59:04,359 --> 01:59:06,699
And I guarantee you, you could take any two people,

2588
01:59:07,139 --> 01:59:08,799
put them in the environment that we're creating.

2589
01:59:09,039 --> 01:59:10,779
They could hate each other politically.

2590
01:59:11,079 --> 01:59:12,779
They could be from opposite ends of the earth.

2591
01:59:12,960 --> 01:59:15,219
And at the end of that, we need to make them love each other.

2592
01:59:15,339 --> 01:59:15,579
Right.

2593
01:59:16,079 --> 01:59:16,659
That's it.

2594
01:59:16,960 --> 01:59:18,159
And so how do you do that?

2595
01:59:18,319 --> 01:59:21,139
Well, creating moments of awe and wonder

2596
01:59:21,139 --> 01:59:23,159
where you feel like you're five years old again

2597
01:59:23,159 --> 01:59:24,699
is what Strange House is about.

2598
01:59:24,939 --> 01:59:27,859
And it's gonna be really hard to build

2599
01:59:27,859 --> 01:59:29,659
and really expensive to build.

2600
01:59:29,779 --> 01:59:32,359
And we found a space, 90,000 square feet,

2601
01:59:32,359 --> 01:59:34,719
underneath Wall Street in Manhattan,

2602
01:59:36,079 --> 01:59:40,420
six months of negotiating the LOI on the lease,

2603
01:59:40,420 --> 01:59:43,639
because when you go to a REIT and you go,

2604
